# A bare ESP32-S3 on a board of its own (build.sh s3direct): TRS TIP on GPIO14 (the data, Type A), RING on GPIO15
# (held high in board_init() as the current source), IN through the 6N137 on GPIO21; 22 ohm in series on each output
# pin. The module is an ESP32-S3-WROOM-1-N16R8, but the 4 MB partition layout stays: it is frozen for OTA and shared
# with the other boards. The console is TinyUSB's serial port on the native USB (CONFIG_ESP_CONSOLE_NONE, from
# sdkconfig.defaults.esp32s3): USB-Serial-JTAG and TinyUSB share the PHY, and anything written there after TinyUSB
# starts hangs the chip. There is no USB-UART bridge on the board.
CONFIG_AIRMIDI_BOARD_DIRECT_S3=y
